course: dictionary
lesson: 2441
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and Dakota is one of them. A capital letter tells you it is a name, but it could be the name of a place, a people, or a person. The words around it tell you which one it is.
explain: Sometimes Dakota is a place. «Children have found important fossils, such as a young T. rex found by boys in North Dakota in 2022.» The sentence is about where something was found, so North Dakota must be a US state.
explain: Sometimes Dakota is a people, as in «the Dakota people». Clues like people, plains and buffalo, which you meet in history lessons, show that it means a group of Native Americans. Ask yourself: is this a place, a group of people, or a person?
explain: Sometimes Dakota is a person's name. «At school a kid sneers at Dakota» tells you a kid is being unkind to someone, so Dakota must be a first name. Always check the clues, because the spelling is the same for all three meanings.
fact: Dakota with a capital letter is a name: it can be a place, a people, or a person.
fact: North Dakota and South Dakota are two states in the middle north of the USA, and together they are called «the Dakotas».
fact: The Dakota people are a Native American people of the Great Plains, part of the Sioux nation. They also have their own language.
fact: Dakota is also used as a first name, as in «At school a kid sneers at Dakota».
fact: Mount Rushmore is in South Dakota.
exercise: «Children have found important fossils, such as a young T. rex found by boys in North Dakota in 2022.» In this sentence, what is Dakota? | A kind of dinosaur | *A US state | A person's first name | A people of the Great Plains
exercise: «The Dakota people lived on the plains and hunted buffalo.» What does Dakota mean here? | Two US states together | A museum in Chicago | *A Native American people of the Great Plains | A first name for a boy
exercise: «At school a kid sneers at Dakota.» Find and copy the word that tells you Dakota is a person. | at | *kid | sneers | school
test: What are «the Dakotas»? | A group of T. rex fossils | *Two US states: North Dakota and South Dakota | Two rivers in Canada | A school in Chicago
test: How can you tell that Dakota is a person's name and not a place? | *The sentence is about someone being spoken to or treated in a certain way | Dakota has more than five letters | Dakota is in the dictionary | Dakota always means a person
exam: Which phrase names a people, not a place? | *the Dakota people | the Dakotas | South Dakota | North Dakota
